investigators in florida released body  camera footage of a wild shootout  between deputies and a boy and girl the  volusa county sheriff's office says the  children  shot at the deputies for more than half  an hour tuesday night before the  deputies returned fire  manuel bejorquez has more on this story  and we do warn you  the video is disturbing  shooting out the rear window toward my  direction stand by that sergeant donnie  maxwell taking  cover behind a tree  he's taking fire from a 12-year-old boy  and a 14-year-old girl from inside the  house  police say the two children had fled  from a juvenile home northeast of  orlando  and broken into this unattended house  finding several large firearms  when police arrived the children opened  fire  put the guns down  10-4 they're shooting at me at one point  in the nine-minute edited video  maxwell with his gun drawn mutters to  himself  appearing to pray for a peaceful outcome  don't let me do this  don't do this more than 30 minutes into  the standoff  aerial footage then appears to capture  police opening fire  the flashing dots are the bullets coming  from the officers assembled behind the  tree  police say they started shooting  striking the girl and wounding her  after she came outside pointing a  shotgun at the officers  the 12-year-old boy who had been  carrying an ak-47  surrenders and the officers rushed to  administer first aid to the girl  it up here now in the whoever none of  the officers were injured despite having  multiple rounds fired at them  but the female suspect was transported  to a local hospital  where she underwent surgery and is in  stable condition  in a statement the juvenile facility  where the children were staying said  these children are in desperate need of  care in the appropriate setting  which is a higher level of care than we  provide  for cbs this morning anwa bajorkas miami
 

